.TH voltkit-rename 1  "Voltkit 0.10.5" "Voltkit Manual"
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
voltkit\-rename \- Rename many files at once: search and replace, regular expressions, numbering and letter case
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBvoltkit rename\fR [\fB\-\-find\fR] [\fB\-\-replace\fR] [\fB\-\-regex\fR] [\fB\-\-ignore\-case\fR] [\fB\-\-first\fR] [\fB\-\-scope\fR] [\fB\-\-case\fR] [\fB\-\-start\fR] [\fB\-\-step\fR] [\fB\-\-apply\fR] [\fB\-\-undo\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIFILE\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shows what would be renamed and changes nothing, until you add \-\-apply. Every conflict (two files getting one name, a name that is taken) is reported first, and a batch is renamed all or nothing. The last batch can be undone with \-\-undo.
.PP
In the replacement, {n} is the file\*(Aqs number and {n:3} is the number padded to 3 digits; with \-\-regex, $1 and ${name} are the groups of the match. An empty \-\-find matches the whole name, so \-\-replace \*(Aqphoto\-{n:3}\*(Aq numbers every file.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-find\fR \fI<FIND>\fR [default: ]
The text to look for (empty matches the whole name)
.TP
\fB\-\-replace\fR \fI<REPLACE>\fR [default: ]
The text to put instead
.TP
\fB\-\-regex\fR
Treat \-\-find as a regular expression
.TP
\fB\-\-ignore\-case\fR
Ignore the difference between upper and lower case when searching
.TP
\fB\-\-first\fR
Replace only the first match in each name
.TP
\fB\-\-scope\fR \fI<SCOPE>\fR [default: name]
Which part of the name to change
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
name: The name without its extension
.IP \(bu 2
extension: Only the extension
.IP \(bu 2
full: The whole name, extension included
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-case\fR \fI<LETTER_CASE>\fR [default: keep]
Change the letter case afterwards
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
keep
.IP \(bu 2
upper
.IP \(bu 2
lower
.IP \(bu 2
title
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-start\fR \fI<START>\fR [default: 1]
The first number for {n}
.TP
\fB\-\-step\fR \fI<STEP>\fR [default: 1]
How much each next file adds to the number
.TP
\fB\-\-apply\fR
Really rename the files; without it only the preview is shown
.TP
\fB\-\-undo\fR
Undo the last batch renamed with \-\-apply (or in the app)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
[\fIFILE\fR]
Files and folders to rename, in the order they are numbered
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
